# Recording with q{reg} and replaying with @{reg} (repeat.txt, complex-repeat).

=== qa records keys and @a replays them
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |abcdef
keys:   qaxq@a
expect: |cdef
regs:   "a = "x"
mode:   normal

=== the q that stops recording isn't stored
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  The 'q' that stops recording is not stored in the register
given:  |one two three
keys:   qadwq
expect: |two three
regs:   "a = "dw"
mode:   normal

=== recording leaves the unnamed register to the commands it records
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |one two three
keys:   qadwq
expect: |two three
regs:   "" = "one "   "- = "one "
mode:   normal

=== recording an insert keeps the <Esc>
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   qaI- <Esc>jq@a
expect:
  - one
  -| two
regs:   "a = "I- \x1bj"
mode:   normal

=== recording an Ex command keeps the <CR>
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:
  |a1
  a2
  a3
keys:   qa:s/a/b/<CR>jq@a
expect:
  b1
  b2
  |a3
regs:   "a = ":s/a/b/\rj"
mode:   normal

=== q in Insert mode is just a character
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |x
keys:   qaiq<Esc>q
expect: |qx
regs:   "a = "iq\x1b"
mode:   normal

=== qA appends to the recording in a
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  (uppercase to append)
given:  |abcdefgh
keys:   qaxqqAxq@a
expect: |efgh
regs:   "a = "xx"
mode:   normal

=== qA appends a recording to a yanked word
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  (uppercase to append)
given:  |foo bar
keys:   "ayiwqA$q
expect: foo ba|r
regs:   "a = "foo$"
mode:   normal

=== qA appends a recording to a yanked line before its newline
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  (uppercase to append)
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   "ayyqAjq
expect:
  one
  |two
regs:   "a = "onej\n"
mode:   normal

=== qaq empties register a
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |foo bar
keys:   "ayiwqaq
expect: |foo bar
regs:   "a = ""
mode:   normal

=== q1 records into a numbered register
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |abcd
keys:   q1xq@1
expect: |cd
regs:   "1 = "x"
mode:   normal

=== a count typed while recording is recorded
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Record typed characters into register {0-9a-zA-Z"}
given:  |abcdefgh
keys:   qa2xq@a
expect: |efgh
regs:   "a = "2x"
mode:   normal

=== a count before q is kept and applies to the key after the replay
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  Stops recording.
given:  |abcdefgh
keys:   qax3q@ax
expect: |fgh
regs:   "a = "x3"
mode:   normal

=== a put of the recorded register gives the keys as text
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  the put will paste the recorded macro
given:  |one two
keys:   qadwq"aP
expect: d|wtwo
regs:   "a = "dw"
mode:   normal

=== q is disabled while executing a register
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  The 'q' command is disabled while executing a register
given:  |qbxq abc
keys:   "ay4lw@a
expect: |bxq abc
regs:   "b = (unset)
mode:   normal

=== q inside :normal records nothing
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *q*
quote:  it doesn't work inside a mapping and |:normal|.
given:  |abc
keys:   :normal qbxq<CR>
expect: |bc
regs:   "b = ""
mode:   normal

=== Q replays the last recorded register
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *Q*
quote:  Repeat the last recorded register [count] times.
given:  |abcdefgh
keys:   qaxqQ
expect: |cdefgh
mode:   normal

=== 2Q replays the last recorded register twice
ref:    nvim/repeat.txt *Q*
quote:  Repeat the last recorded register [count] times.
given:  |abcdefgh
keys:   qbxq2Q
expect: |defgh
mode:   normal
